From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:49:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 117/138] experimental (not deployed): token-space moe_align +
 VLLM_EXP_TOPK_FIRST sampler path

- moe_align_block_size small-batch kernel rewritten in token-slot space (sort,
  segment scans, numel <= ALIGN_MAX_NUMEL = 256): 6.9 -> 4.4 us at 80 slots,
  5.1 at 160, tie at 320, 13.6 vs 7.0 at 640 (W25). Select with
  VLLM_EXP_MOE_SMALL=sum,align.
- VLLM_EXP_TOPK_FIRST=1: top-k-first top-k/top-p (torch.topk of the largest
  per-row top-k, values cut-off). Masks identical to the Triton kernel and the
  sort reference, but torch.topk over 248K logits is itself ~360 us: no faster
  at 8 rows (360 vs 377 us), slower at 32-48 rows. Left off.

W25 server (p7 config + sum,align): greedy single 297.4/128.9/395.6 vs p7
298.9/128.7/396.8 (no measurable change), probes token-identical, NaN poke
clean, GSM8K 96.5 (120 s, 490 tok/s), 0 runtime errors. Production stays p7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
